{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301354-anyone-else-started-a-lunars-game-or-a-game-with-lots-of-lunars","id":1301354,"title":"Anyone else started a Lunars game? Or a game with lots of Lunars?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-31T11:07:23-07:00","id":1301354,"title":"Anyone else started a Lunars game? Or a game with lots of Lunars?","content":"Now the book is fully out, I'm just interested.<br /> What's your story like;<br /> how have you found it different than running a mainly-Solars game;<br /> what have you done with Shahan-yas;<br /> what kind of characters have you got;<br /> etc?<br /> What do you think of the Role bonuses for Lunar XP? I'm a little worried about characters who are obviously going to be one Caste, but aren't yet tattooed, getting less Role XP. Not a big worry, but a little one.<br /> <br /> I've run one session so far of my game Heroes of the Frozen North.<br /> <br /> We've got:<br /> Olaf Keelbreaker, the Steel Iceberg - Full Moon with a Walrus totem and a grimscythe made of his own tusk;<br /> Amira, a beautiful merchant's daughter who lies at the heart of the social web - Changing Moon spider-totem<br /> Atal, a shaman from the swamp with Charisma 1 who just wants to make friends - No Moon with a toad-totem<br /> Mujin, an exotic foreign merchant (apparently) - Casteless with a polecat-totem<br /> Underfoot, a feral man from the jungle - Casteless with a gorilla-totem<br /> There's also a red panda who is most definitely not a Changing Moon-caste Lunar, and able to say so with Glance-Oration Technique.<br /> <br /> So, to my surprise, I've ended up with one combat Lunar, one all-rounder, one shaman, and three social characters. How have other players/ST found it? One of the players wondered if people play Lunars as social characters more (in our mixed Celestial games, social Lunars are fairly common), but I think it's more just coincidence.<br /> <br /> I brought them together with a couple of NPCs for a moot, but I didn't really give anyone a Shahan-Ya. I would've if anyone showed interest; but they didn't. No-one took Mentor. Or Ally 5 for a Solar Mate either, actually.<br /> <br /> The moot was a party at the castle of King Arcturus, a Changing Moon who'd united warring clans, which I think worked well with all the social characters, but maybe wouldn't if I'd had a bunch of smelly barbarians.<br /> <br /> I also have to say that the character gen system seemed to work better than for Solars; everyone seems quite balanced, there's no-one with a ton of Abilities at 5 or Willpower 10 or anything. Though that might be the maturity of my players compared to when old games started years ago.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-31-2019, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T01:19:47-07:00","id":1301550,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the main strength of the Changing and No Moons is that if you max Dex and turn into a scary or flying animal, it doesn\u2019t matter what your Str and Sta is like, you are still about as combat competent as a Full Moon (ish).<br /> <br /> So I see a lot of Changing and No Moons from an Optimization angle as you are really good at your thing and you have an invincible battle-form when you need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T02:06:24-07:00","id":1301554,"title":"","content":"As one of the players in Oz's game I was going to play a big, strong Full Moon but didn't want to step on Underfoot and Olaf's toes, and had already sold myself on a new concept by the time I realised it was going to be rammed full of social characters. Incidentally I think only one, at best, of the socialites has a worthwhile animal shape to battle in.<br /> <br /> I found it very interesting that almost every player gravitated towards making use of particular attributes and others are significantly underrepresented, there's a lot of Strength, Appearance and Charisma charms going around and very little in the way of Dexterity for example, so it certainly seems some charm trees are more engaging than others, for this group at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T08:39:35-07:00","id":1301639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301354-anyone-else-started-a-lunars-game-or-a-game-with-lots-of-lunars?p=1301550#post1301550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the main strength of the Changing and No Moons is that if you max Dex and turn into a scary or flying animal, it doesn\u2019t matter what your Str and Sta is like, you are still about as combat competent as a Full Moon (ish).<br /> <br /> So I see a lot of Changing and No Moons from an Optimization angle as you are really good at your thing and you have an invincible battle-form when you need.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that might happen, but actually it hasn't really.<br /> <br /> Most people have Dex 3 and Brawl 1. 4 of the 6 PCs have other combat abilities higher than their Brawl. For example, the character with the most forms has Brawl 1, Archery 3, and a Powerbow. Yes, she can turn into a bear, but she's clearly designed for archery.<br /> <br /> Fodor's character is actually the only character really optimised for taking advantage of shape-changing into animals, and even they only have Brawl 2, which isn't that high.<br /> <br /> It might be that my players either a)didn't really get how shapeshifting works (it is a bit complex), or b)weren't that fussed about optimising characters. At least, for combat (as many are social characters).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fodor</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ... had already sold myself on a new concept by the time I realised it was going to be rammed full of social characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I wondered if it's just coincidence. With 6 players, I'd expect 2 physical characters, 2 social characters, and 2 mental characters. 3 social characters, 1 physical, 1 mental, and 1 all-rounder doesn't seem far-out.<br /> So I wondered how many Changing Moons other people have in their games.<br /> <br /> In the other two games I play:<br /> One has a social-primary Casteless and a physical/mental Casteless<br /> One has a Changing Moon and used to have a No Moon as well<br /> <br /> So this is partly why my friend who plays that Changing Moon wondered if Changing Moons are much more popular than other Castes, and I'm interested in what other groups have found.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> there's a lot of Strength, Appearance and Charisma charms going around and very little in the way of Dexterity </div> </div> </div>True. One PC has lots of Manipulation, one has lots of Intelligence charms, and one Wits. But no one's got more than 1 or 2 Dexterity and Perception charms.<br /> <br /> When I play Lunars, I always take a ton of Perception charms for tracking, reading people, etc, but no one else seems to.<br /> <br /> If I look at the Favoured Attributes PCs have:<br /> Str x2<br /> Dex x4<br /> Sta x2<br /> Cha x2<br /> Man x2<br /> App x2<br /> Per x2<br /> Int x1<br /> Wits x3<br /> <br /> Interestingly, that looks like Dex and Wits are really popular, but most people have like 1 Dexterity charm; I think they picked it either conceptually, or for the excellency! But it might mean that in 10 sessions time, it's a bit more popular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-01-2019, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T10:57:55-07:00","id":1301693,"title":"","content":"I can\u2019t believe you miss classed FODORs Ambush Predator as a social character ! Our own night caste equivalent . Tsk tsk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T11:45:19-07:00","id":1301704,"title":"","content":"Possibly it\u2019s a bit skewed by the chargen rules for Lunars.<br /> <br /> For Solars, it\u2019s not really feasible to take 15 non-caste/favored charms at chargen, so that you get every Excellency and, even if you did, you probably wouldn\u2019t have particularly good pools everywhere.<br /> <br /> For Lunars, you have 4 caste/favored abilities where you\u2019re almost certainly getting an Excellency for free already. For the other five Attributes, it\u2019s difficult to not have enough dots in them to pick up two charms each for most of them. And, since you can boost your excellency cap by 5, because you have at least one Attribute at 5, it means that there\u2019s a real incentive to start with, like, six or more unfavored charms.<br /> <br /> I mean, my Lunar has 7 of 9 Excellencies. But I\u2019m planning to focus mainly on Int and App charms in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T12:10:58-07:00","id":1301706,"title":"","content":"So I'm currently running a primarily Lunar game for my gaming group as part of our rotation of games. (We have something like 4 or 5 games in rotation at the moment.) I say primarily Lunar because one of our members hates making characters and wasn't especially jazzed for Lunars, but the rest of the group was chomping at the bit for them. So as a compromise we let her bring back a Solar character from a previous campaign. We've only got about 1 session under our belt at the moment.<br /> <br /> Our cast of characters is:<br /> Hardack, the Vegetarian Behemoth. A proud and intimidating Ox-Dragon Totem Full Moon who stands tall even as a mouse and beats enemies into submission with his wide array of animal forms.<br /> T'elm, the quote &quot;Monstrous Blue Mage.&quot; This Casteless Polar Bear Totem spends most his time as a bear devouring people and monsters and taking their power for himself. He is close friends with Hardack.<br /> Oct, an Octopus Folk Ninja and Historian. An Octopus Totem No Moon who collects and spreads knowledge while commanding an army of beastfolk ninja from his homeland the village hidden in the waves.<br /> Meurta, the apprentice of the Ghost King. Meurta is a Twilight caste sorcerer* who the rest of the Circle is convinced is an Abyssal due to her obsession with ghosts and apprenticeship to a mysterious ancient ghost that sounds a lot like a Deathlord.<br /> And finally Nafulla the beautiful seductress and martial artist. This Spider Totem Changing Moon is a consummate manipulator who has infiltrated the Bureau of Destiny and plays them and the Silver Pact against each other for her own ends. Her only true allegiance being to her Shahan-Ya's ideology.<br /> <br /> Our game is set in the Southwest, a fair ways north of the Cinder Isles but till south of An-Teng. And our first little story hook has been them dealing with some &quot;advance scouts&quot; from the army of Spear-Empress Bhadri. Which they got involved with initially because these advance scouts were devouring all of the spirits in the areas they passed through, including Ghosts. And this right riled up Meurta, and as Nafulla's Shahan-Ya had requested that the rest of the Circle keep an eye on the &quot;Abyssal&quot; operating in the area they got brought along for the ride. They however became personally invested once they noticed the atrocities the Fae were committing to humans as well. I have plans to work in Solar Mates for a few of the characters who wanted them, but they have not shown up yet and the players established they have not yet met their Solar Mates. Though a couple of them had some very specific notes on what they wanted.<br /> <br /> As for how I've found this different from a solar game. It's a bit early to say. There was a scene where a couple of the group split of to hunt forms specific to the needs of the situation. (Large forms to carry the children they saved to safety.) Also the party seems just a lot more anti-Realm than our previous Solar games. Where they always found some way of at least trying to work with portions of the Realm in a positive manor. This however hasn't been a huge point yet, as they haven't yet interacted with the Realm in game. But it will come up. I think the biggest thing I've noticed is how all of the Lunar characters really tie back into some aspect of the Lunar themes. T'elm is perhaps the best example, or at least easiest to quantify. T'elm is just straight up a monster, he would tell you so himself. But he's a monster that aids people in need and becomes enraged by sadistic cruelty. He really captures a uniquely Lunar feeling of the Monster red in tooth and claw who some might still view as a protector or savior.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*Note Meurta would have been a Necromancer if there were rules for it. But there are not, so instead she just is a sorcerer with a custom initiation and a custom Ghost Summoning spell.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/112-sanguine","name":"Sanguine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar112_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T19:49:37-07:00","id":1301789,"title":"","content":"I've got a Solar/Lunar mixed game: 3 Solars, 3 Lunars. We just started today (and are doing PBP) so we haven't done much yet, but...<br /> <br /> One of the Lunars flirts with the fire elemental in her grill to help make the perfect burger and - because of the dice this adds - it is so good that I had to actively fight the urge to describe it as tasting like an orgasm in a second Lunar's mouth. (She got like 5 10s!!) This was *after* flirting with the Lunar to get him interested in trying her burgers in the first place.<br /> <br /> Exalted is a *weird* game but I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T08:11:36-07:00","id":1301913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301354-anyone-else-started-a-lunars-game-or-a-game-with-lots-of-lunars?p=1301789#post1301789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted is a *weird* game but I like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah, no argument there.<br /> What are the 3 Lunars?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T08:16:00-07:00","id":1301915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanguine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301354-anyone-else-started-a-lunars-game-or-a-game-with-lots-of-lunars?p=1301706#post1301706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm currently running a primarily Lunar game for my gaming group as part of our rotation of games. (We have something like 4 or 5 games in rotation at the moment.) ... We've only got about 1 session under our belt at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we do the same. That's why we've only got 1 session done so far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Our cast of characters is:<br /> Hardack, the Vegetarian Behemoth. A proud and intimidating Ox-Dragon Totem Full Moon who stands tall even as a mouse and beats enemies into submission with his wide array of animal forms.<br /> T'elm, the quote &quot;Monstrous Blue Mage.&quot; This Casteless Polar Bear Totem spends most his time as a bear devouring people and monsters and taking their power for himself. He is close friends with Hardack.<br /> Oct, an Octopus Folk Ninja and Historian. An Octopus Totem No Moon who collects and spreads knowledge while commanding an army of beastfolk ninja from his homeland the village hidden in the waves.<br /> Meurta, the apprentice of the Ghost King. Meurta is a Twilight caste sorcerer* who the rest of the Circle is convinced is an Abyssal due to her obsession with ghosts and apprenticeship to a mysterious ancient ghost that sounds a lot like a Deathlord.<br /> And finally Nafulla the beautiful seductress and martial artist. This Spider Totem Changing Moon is a consummate manipulator who has infiltrated the Bureau of Destiny and plays them and the Silver Pact against each other for her own ends. Her only true allegiance being to her Shahan-Ya's ideology. </div> </div> </div>Sounds quite balanced. And it doesn't sound like the characters have much cross-over in terms of what they've bought?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Our game is set in the Southwest, a fair ways north of the Cinder Isles but till south of An-Teng. </div> </div> </div>That was actually my second choice for somewhere to set the game.<br /> I think possibly Lunar games make people think of somewhere deep in the Threshold. And having played Exalted for years, there's the urge to set the game somewhere other than the usual suspects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for how I've found this different from a solar game. It's a bit early to say. There was a scene where a couple of the group split of to hunt forms specific to the needs of the situation. (Large forms to carry the children they saved to safety.) Also the party seems just a lot more anti-Realm than our previous Solar games. Where they always found some way of at least trying to work with portions of the Realm in a positive manor. This however hasn't been a huge point yet, as they haven't yet interacted with the Realm in game. But it will come up. I think the biggest thing I've noticed is how all of the Lunar characters really tie back into some aspect of the Lunar themes. T'elm is perhaps the best example, or at least easiest to quantify. T'elm is just straight up a monster, he would tell you so himself. But he's a monster that aids people in need and becomes enraged by sadistic cruelty. He really captures a uniquely Lunar feeling of the Monster red in tooth and claw who some might still view as a protector or savior. </div> </div> </div>Hmmm...<br /> Yeah, I don't think I've found mine massively different so far. But the first session was at a royal court, which maybe isn't a particularly &quot;Lunar&quot; place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T08:18:05-07:00","id":1301917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanguine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301354-anyone-else-started-a-lunars-game-or-a-game-with-lots-of-lunars?p=1301706#post1301706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Our game is set in the Southwest, a fair ways north of the Cinder Isles but till south of An-Teng. And our first little story hook has been them dealing with some &quot;advance scouts&quot; from the army of Spear-Empress Bhadri. Which they got involved with initially because these advance scouts were devouring all of the spirits in the areas they passed through, including Ghosts. And this right riled up Meurta, and as Nafulla's Shahan-Ya had requested that the rest of the Circle keep an eye on the &quot;Abyssal&quot; operating in the area they got brought along for the ride. They however became personally invested once they noticed the atrocities the Fae were committing to humans as well. I have plans to work in Solar Mates for a few of the characters who wanted them, but they have not shown up yet and the players established they have not yet met their Solar Mates. Though a couple of them had some very specific notes on what they wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any plans for encounters with the cadet House Yueh?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T09:20:48-07:00","id":1301925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301354-anyone-else-started-a-lunars-game-or-a-game-with-lots-of-lunars?p=1301913#post1301913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hah, no argument there.<br /> What are the 3 Lunars?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually the grill lunar in that game. Etana is a changing moon with strength favored and intelligence favored. She uses charisma and appearance. She has the giant merit and her totem is an auroch. Her story is fun in that she basically Green Eggs and Hammed luna until luna finally tried this &quot;Burger&quot; thing and gave her an exaltation (she was actually on her way to exalt someone else)<br /> She is a capitalist and very much into profit and cooking.<br /> <br /> We have another changing moon who is more the manipulator (that's the one my character got to try the burger). He's an albatross totem and very good at keeping secrets (high guile and manipulation) but not very resolute (low wits and integrity)<br /> <br /> Our other lunar is a no moon sorcerer mated to our dawn, they for ma battle couple as the dawn is a commander and the no moon is a djala ladybug totem with a large army.<br /> <br /> Our solars are the war supernal dawn, a twilight occultist, and a twilight crafter.<br /> <br /> Exalted is weird and I love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T11:54:46-07:00","id":1301963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301354-anyone-else-started-a-lunars-game-or-a-game-with-lots-of-lunars?p=1301913#post1301913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hah, no argument there.<br /> What are the 3 Lunars?</div> </div> </div> </div>What Kell_Tamer said, though I'll note the Ladybug sees herself as being more of a field commander while the Dawn works in the back on an overall strategy.<br /> <br /> The Aurochs is probably the most &quot;out-there&quot; of all our characters. We have a prodigy general (Dawn), a field commander freeing slaves (Ladybug), a sorcerer folk hero (Twilight Occultist), a crafter of a brand new material with a fire elemental familiar (Twilight Craftsman), a scout who survived being marooned (Seagull)... and a cow lady running a successful food stand through the power of cheeseburgers and sex appeal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T14:48:47-07:00","id":1302016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301354-anyone-else-started-a-lunars-game-or-a-game-with-lots-of-lunars?p=1301915#post1301915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds quite balanced. And it doesn't sound like the characters have much cross-over in terms of what they've bought?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. We've got a pretty nice spread of things. There is some overlap in attributes. Hardack and T'elm both have a fair amount of investment in Stamina for instance, though it's not either players primary focus. But within those attributes people have mostly picked up different trees. Aside from a few bread and butter Charms like Ox-Body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301354-anyone-else-started-a-lunars-game-or-a-game-with-lots-of-lunars?p=1301917#post1301917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any plans for encounters with the cadet House Yueh?</div> </div> </div> </div>In all honesty I had forgotten about them. But now that you've reminded me. Yeah definitely gonna plan some stuff with House Yueh, they are a perfect fit. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/112-sanguine","name":"Sanguine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar112_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T14:52:49-07:00","id":1302017,"title":"","content":"Cadet House Yueh? I can't remember them. Is that something in What Fire Has Wrought?<br /> <br /> <br /> I think Stamina, being a defensive attribute, is probably something lots of people have a bit of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T18:48:23-07:00","id":1302078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301354-anyone-else-started-a-lunars-game-or-a-game-with-lots-of-lunars?p=1302017#post1302017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cadet House Yueh? I can't remember them. Is that something in What Fire Has Wrought?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be the place for cadet Houses, yes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanguine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301354-anyone-else-started-a-lunars-game-or-a-game-with-lots-of-lunars?p=1302016#post1302016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In all honesty I had forgotten about them.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I only just recalled them a couple of days ago when I went to review the cadet Houses for... personal reasons. The description of an island satrapy made me think Southwest (which was the Direction I was looking to see if there was any associated cadet House), and upon reviewing the map I took note of how Goldenseal was a spot located somewhere about halfway between An-Teng and the Cinder Isles, which I believe has thus far not been detailed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T13:36:18-07:00","id":1304014,"title":"","content":"I just (last night) started running a Lunar game. We spent about half the session so we didn't actually do much yet, but one of the characters did get to show off how the Lunar's Excellency calculation can let you go nuts if you're willing to spend the personal motes for it.<br /> <br /> Only one character, the Full Moon, has a close relationship with their Sahan-Ya (they picked Rukhsara-who-Remembers) and the other two PCs are more nomadic. The Changing Moon is a Single Point stylist, the Full Moon is low dex but uses the strength and stamina replacer charms, and the No Moon is a sorceress because of course. The Changing Moon is an oddly overt sort, going very Pretty Kitty (well, Pretty Puppy, with her wolf totem) with a tendency to wander around in hybrid form pretending to be a godblood and keeping her sword always ready to whip out for Shining Point. The Full Moon is more or less a paladin filtered through the lens of Exalted, carrying on their former role as a town watchman writ large (with the added benefit of now being able to fully express their genderfluidity). They're also the only one with Appearance less than 5, because, well, That's My Table*. Then you have the No Moon sorceress who <i>also</i> goes Pretty Kitty but in her case it's Pretty Birdie, as she has a raiton totem and goes full sexy gothy witch.<br /> <br /> Since it's easy to top out a few attributes and hard to do it with skills,they strongly favored that.<br /> <br /> We haven't done much yet. The Lunar who summoned them to help is pretending to be an ex-slave sent to guide them to take their measure, which the No Moon blew up the Perception Excellency to Read Intentions through.<br /> <br /> *You'd think we're a bunch of creepy neckbeards but I'm the only guy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T14:05:05-07:00","id":1304023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301354-anyone-else-started-a-lunars-game-or-a-game-with-lots-of-lunars?p=1304014#post1304014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">with a tendency to wander around in hybrid form pretending to be a godblood</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a bad idea. I've generally found PCs pretending to be god-bloods works much better than pretending to be mortals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're also the only one with Appearance less than 5, because, well, That's My Table </div> </div> </div>At one point in 2nd ed, we had two PCs with Appearance 8 and two with Appearance 7.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}